# Whoever did not write it, reviews it.
#
# GitHub never requests a review from the author, so listing both names against
# every path means exactly one thing: every pull request goes to the other person.
# That is the board's rule, "you are the mandatory reviewer in every group whose
# decision you do not own", expressed as the only thing a path file can express.
#
# Deliberately not split by path. Decision ownership is per group and it moves
# between sprints; file ownership would have to be rewritten to stay true, and a
# CODEOWNERS file that has drifted is worse than none. A narrower rule is also a
# trap: naming one owner on a path removes the second reviewer for every change
# that owner writes.
#
# This file requests reviewers. It does not stop a push to main. That takes branch
# protection with "require a pull request" and "require review from Code Owners".

